 "captions": [
  [
   0.0,
   0.799,
   "Part five."
  ],
  [
   0.799,
   1.597,
   "Noisy channels."
  ],
  [
   2.229,
   5.423,
   "Everything so far assumed our bits arrive exactly"
  ],
  [
   5.423,
   7.021,
   "as they were sent."
  ],
  [
   7.021,
   10.215,
   "But the real world is not so tidy."
  ],
  [
   10.215,
   11.014,
   "Wires crackle."
  ],
  [
   11.014,
   11.812,
   "Signals fade."
  ],
  [
   11.812,
   13.41,
   "Bits flip in transit."
  ],
  [
   14.041,
   17.236,
   "This is where Shannon reached his most astonishing"
  ],
  [
   17.236,
   20.43,
   "result of all \u2014 and rewrote what engineers"
  ],
  [
   20.43,
   21.628,
   "believed was possible."
  ],
  [
   22.128,
   24.117,
   "Every real communication channel is noisy."
  ],
  [
   24.117,
   25.111,
   "A radio link,"
  ],
  [
   25.111,
   26.106,
   "a phone line,"
  ],
  [
   26.106,
   27.763,
   "a scratch on a DVD,"
  ],
  [
   27.763,
   29.752,
   "a fading signal from a spacecraft."
  ],
  [
   30.384,
   33.036,
   "To reason about all of them at once,"
  ],
  [
   33.036,
   35.687,
   "we strip the idea down to its bones"
  ],
  [
   35.687,
   38.339,
   "\u2014 the simplest model of noise there is,"
  ],
  [
   38.339,
   39.665,
   "the binary symmetric channel."
  ],
  [
   40.297,
   41.954,
   "Here is how it works."
  ],
  [
   41.954,
   43.943,
   "You send a single bit in."
  ],
  [
   43.943,
   45.269,
   "Most of the time,"
  ],
  [
   45.269,
   47.589,
   "it comes out the other side unchanged."
  ],
  [
   47.589,
   49.247,
   "But with some fixed probability,"
  ],
  [
   49.247,
   50.573,
   "the noise flips it."
  ],
  [
   50.573,
   52.562,
   "A zero arrives as a one."
  ],
  [
   52.562,
   54.551,
   "A one arrives as a zero."
  ],
  [
   55.182,
   56.177,
   "Watch the stream."
  ],
  [
   56.177,
   57.171,
   "On the left,"
  ],
  [
   57.171,
   58.497,
   "the sender pushes clean,"
  ],
  [
   58.497,
   60.154,
   "deliberate bits into the channel."
  ],
  [
   60.786,
   61.117,
   "Inside,"
  ],
  [
   61.117,
   62.443,
   "noise strikes at random,"
  ],
  [
   62.443,
   65.095,
   "sparking here and there with no pattern you"
  ],
  [
   65.095,
   65.758,
   "can predict."
  ],
  [
   66.39,
   67.716,
   "And on the right,"
  ],
  [
   67.716,
   69.705,
   "the receiver reads out whatever survived."
  ],
  [
   69.705,
   72.357,
   "A few of those bits are now wrong"
  ],
  [
   72.357,
   74.345,
   "\u2014 flipped \u2014 marked in red."
  ],
  [
   74.977,
   77.297,
   "Now here is the genuinely cruel part,"
  ],
  [
   77.297,
   79.286,
   "the thing that makes this hard."
  ],
  [
   79.286,
   81.938,
   "The receiver has no way of knowing which"
  ],
  [
   81.938,
   82.601,
   "bits flipped."
  ],
  [
   83.233,
   85.885,
   "A received one looks utterly identical whether it"
  ],
  [
   85.885,
   87.542,
   "was sent as a one,"
  ],
  [
   87.542,
   90.194,
   "or sent as a zero and corrupted along"
  ],
  [
   90.194,
   90.857,
   "the way."
  ],
  [
   90.857,
   92.183,
   "The damage is invisible."
  ],
  [
   92.814,
   94.472,
   "So it looks completely hopeless."
  ],
  [
   94.472,
   96.792,
   "If any bit can silently betray you,"
  ],
  [
   96.792,
   98.781,
   "and you can never tell which,"
  ],
  [
   98.781,
   101.433,
   "how could you ever communicate reliably at all?"
  ],
  [
   102.064,
   102.727,
   "For years,"
  ],
  [
   102.727,
   105.048,
   "the smartest engineers believed you simply\ncouldn't."
  ],
  [
   105.048,
   107.7,
   "They were convinced that noise imposed a permanent"
  ],
  [
   107.7,
   109.689,
   "ceiling \u2014 that to cut errors,"
  ],
  [
   109.689,
   112.34,
   "you had to slow down toward a crawl,"
  ],
  [
   112.34,
   114.992,
   "and even then a little noise always leaked"
  ],
  [
   114.992,
   115.324,
   "through."
  ],
  [
   115.955,
   118.276,
   "Shannon proved every one of them wrong."
  ],
  [
   118.276,
   120.928,
   "And the way he did it is the"
  ],
  [
   120.928,
   123.248,
   "most beautiful surprise in the whole subject."
  ]
